@startuml components
title Trade Store - how the pieces fit together

actor Client

package "app" {
  component "main.py\n(FastAPI endpoints,\nTradeIn model,\nget_conn / get_today)" as Main
  component "rules.py\n(check_maturity_date,\ndecide_action, is_expired,\nexceptions)" as Rules
  component "db.py\n(sqlite3 functions)" as DB
  component "scheduler.py\n(expiry job: at startup +\ndaily after midnight)" as Sched
}

database "SQLite file\ntrades.db" as SQLite

artifact "Open-source dependencies\n(requirements*.txt +\npackages they pull in)" as Deps

package "tests" {
  component "test_rules.py" as TRules
  component "test_db.py" as TDB
  component "test_api.py\n+ conftest.py" as TAPI
  component "test_scheduler.py" as TSched
}

package "GitHub Actions (ci.yml)" {
  component "Job: Regression tests\n(pytest)" as CITest
  component "Job: Vulnerability scan\n(pip freeze + Trivy,\nfail on CRITICAL)" as CIScan
}

Client --> Main : HTTP\nPOST /trades\nGET /trades\nGET /trades/{trade_id}\nGET /health
Main --> Rules : validate trade
Main --> DB : read / write trades
Main --> Sched : starts on startup
Sched --> DB : mark matured\ntrades expired
DB --> SQLite : SQL

TRules ..> Rules : unit tests
TDB ..> DB : tests on a temporary database
TAPI ..> Main : tests through TestClient

CITest ..> TRules : runs
CITest ..> TDB : runs
CITest ..> TAPI : runs
CITest ..> TSched : runs
TSched ..> Sched : tests job + startup
CIScan ..> Deps : scans for\nvulnerabilities

@enduml
